OL,3,AElon Musk appears to signal the end of
OL,4,Athe road for Cybertruck
OL,5,
OL,6,FTesla will wind down production of its
OL,7,FCybertruck vehicles at its Texas
OL,8,Ffactory next year, Elon Musk says.
OL,10,FHe did not spell out whether it plans
OL,11,Fto stop making them entirely or shift
OL,12,Fproduction elsewhere, but did say the
OL,13,Fdecision was to "make room" for
OL,14,Fbuilding more of its self-driving
OL,15,FCybercab cars.
OL,17,FBut the project's lead engineer, Wes
OL,18,FMorrill, appeared to suggest the
OL,19,Fvehicle was being discontinued, writing
OL,20,Fon X: "Cybertruck was an incredible
OL,21,Ftechnology development platform and
OL,22,Flives on through Cybercab."
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
